I have a GBA and flash cart, and use it for a lot of non-GBA-intended 
stuff like emulators. I would *hate* to try to play Nethack on it.
Nethack is very keyboard oriented, and it's hardly even enjoyable to 
play the Smartphone port of it (though I do occasionally, being an 
addict).
For things that port nicely to systems where the entire input system 
consists of six buttons and a directional pad, the GBA is wonderful.

The reason why this is an even worse idea is that you will quickly run 
out of SRAM (or other backup memory) space on the cart, due to the huge 
amount of temporary data that needs to be stored by Nethack even for a 
single game (when you have played a while). But if you only wanted to 
play the early game it would be feasible of course.

